Z||000000||1FST2M6||06-07-2000||08:53 AM||||Well $5.90 for a set of Federal Mogul +.01 con rod bearings and 4.5 hours worth the work my car after about 20 minutes of running... and 30 minutes of nice driving around town I can now TACH it up to above red line again, slide around the neighborhood and pick fights with MOOStangs!!  Still for sale... working on a trade with Jeff for auto GT... but the car works GREAT!! no knock, the rod bearing on #5 had spun and LUCKILY I had only driven about 10 minutes with this TERRIBLE noise.. so I was able to hit the crank with some emory cloth (easy to bend sand paper) and clean up any deposits that were there...  then hit it with 400 grit to polish it up... hi the rest of the mating surfaces with the 400 grit, poped in the new bearings with a little assembly lube and buttoned it all back up... had to take the front motor mount off the block... puled the coil wire off the car spun it over till i got oil pressure back up to 30psi replaced the coil wire and   POOF! no knock, smooth idle, and a sense of accomplishment... went to Taco Mac and had a Black & Tan and 20 HOT wings...   Special Thanks to Ramona at Engineered Performance for putting the oil pan back on... with OUT leaking!   (never have been able to figure that out... lame cork gasket) NO SILICONE!   <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A> ||||reg||1
